Usage: gccli challenges adhoc create --type=STRING <name> [flags]

Create an ad-hoc challenge and invite people who follow you and whom you follow.

Arguments:
  <name>    Challenge name.

Flags:
  -h, --help                     Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json                     Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain                    Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header                   Print the column names as the first line of
                                 --plain output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"             Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING           Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"             Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                                 elevations and weights in table and plain
                                 output: auto (Garmin profile), metric,
                                 statute_us, statute_uk ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version                  Print version information.

      --type=STRING              Activity: walking, running, cycling, swimming,
                                 steps, pushes or pushing-distance.
      --duration="week"          Length: day, weekend (Saturday and Sunday),
                                 week (7 days), month (to the end of the month)
                                 or custom (to --end).
      --start=DATE               First day (YYYY-MM-DD, today, +3d). Default:
                                 today, the Saturday of this week for weekend,
                                 the first day of this month for month.
      --end=DATE                 Last day. Only with --duration custom, at most
                                 60 days after the first day.
      --description=FREE-TEXT    Description. Defaults to the name, because
                                 Garmin requires one.
      --invite=DISPLAY-NAME      Display name of a person who follows you and
                                 whom you follow. Repeat it to invite more
                                 people.

